<title>HUNGARY: ADtranz-96 oper profit after deprec 129 mln ecu.</title>
<headline>ADtranz-96 oper profit after deprec 129 mln ecu.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of European Currency Units unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after depreciation 129     vs NA</p>
<p>    Group sales				  3,196   vs NA</p>
<p>    Order backlog (Dec 31, 1996)	   9,000   vs NA</p>
<p>    Orders received			    3,043   vs NA</p>
<p>    Workforce (headcount)		    21,841  vs NA</p>
<p>NOTE - ABB Daimler-Benz Transportation GmbH (ADtranz) is a 50-50 railway joint venture between Swiss/Swedish company ABB Asea Brown Boveri Ltd and Daimler-Benz AG . The company was founded on January 1, 1996. It calculates its results according to International Accounting Standards (IAS). A company spokesman said that based on IAS, it achieved an eight percent return on capital employed in 1996.</p>
<p>--Scott Miller, Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
